  "reason": "The assistant provides incorrect factual information that contradicts the reference material, including the retirement age (66 instead of 65) and the effective date of the reform (January 1, 2022 instead of January 1, 2024).",
  "evidence": "Under the AHV 21 reform in Switzerland, both men and women receive their AHV (Alters- und Hinterlassenenversicherung) pension at the age of **66**. The reform, which came into effect on January 1, 2022, aimed to equalize the retirement age for both genders, eliminating the previous difference where women could retire earlier."
